edit("docs/implementation-guide.md", [
    ("ledger audit additions",
     "Maintain one source record per primary work in the existing Citation Validation Ledger. Record source identity, the exact complete-text artifact or location inspected, access and inspection state, inspector, and date at the source level. Inside that source record, maintain one claim-evidence mapping for each exact project or manuscript proposition that cites the work. Each mapping records the exact proposition, manuscript or project location, evidence locator, concise support note, scope or caveat, validator and date, second check, User disposition, and mapping status. A paper is never \"validated\" in the abstract: validation applies to a specific source-claim mapping. One validated mapping does not confer validation on another claim citing the same paper.",
     "Maintain one source record per primary work in the existing Citation Validation Ledger. Record source identity, the exact complete-text artifact inspected, source version or edition, immutable version identifier or content digest, access and inspection state, inspector, and date at the source level. Evidence locators are interpreted only against that pinned source version. Inside that source record, maintain one claim-evidence mapping for each exact project or manuscript proposition that cites the work. Each mapping records the stable Claim ID, original and current proposition where applicable, Claim Control Object revision/digest, source version pin, evidence locator, concise support note, scope or caveat, validator and date, blinded second check, User disposition, and mapping status. A paper is never \"validated\" in the abstract: validation applies to a specific source-claim mapping. One validated mapping does not confer validation on another claim citing the same paper.\n\nFor the citation second check, expose the reviewer to the exact Claim ID/proposition and pinned primary source, but not the first validator's locator, evidence note, caveat, or disposition. The reviewer first records an independent locator, paraphrase, caveat, and disposition from the complete primary text; only then compare the two assessments. Record any earlier exposure explicitly and do not label an exposed check independent.\n\nFor manuscript-linked claims, maintain a versioned Claim Control Object keyed by stable Claim ID. It records the current proposition, manuscript file and stable anchor, citation mapping, and claim lineage together with a repository revision or equivalent version and cryptographic digest. When audit narrows wording, retain the same Claim ID if the scientific identity is preserved and store both original and current wording. Citation-only edits, moved text, and narrowed wording update the control object so they remain visible in the same version/diff chain."),
])

edit("docs/record-and-review.md", [
    ("review mapping discipline",
     "Validate citations at the **source-claim mapping** level. The Citation Validation Ledger keeps one source record per primary work, but every exact manuscript or project proposition has its own evidence locator, support note, scope or caveat, checks, and User disposition. Do not infer support for one proposition from a different validated mapping to the same paper, and do not treat complete-text access or inspection as source-wide scientific validation. Reviewers should be able to recover the exact supporting passage or element from the recorded locator without reconstructing the claim from memory.",
     "Validate citations at the **source-claim mapping** level. The Citation Validation Ledger keeps one source record per primary work, but every exact manuscript or project proposition has its own stable Claim ID, pinned source version, evidence locator, support note, scope or caveat, checks, and User disposition. Pin every locator to the exact complete-primary-text version inspected using an immutable version identifier or content digest. Do not infer support for one proposition from a different validated mapping to the same paper, and do not treat complete-text access or inspection as source-wide scientific validation. Reviewers should be able to recover the exact supporting passage or element from the recorded locator and pinned source without reconstructing the claim from memory.\n\nThe citation second check is prospectively blinded. Before seeing the first validator's locator, evidence note, caveat, or disposition, the second participant receives the exact Claim ID/proposition and pinned source, inspects the primary text independently, and durably records their own locator, paraphrase, caveat, and disposition. Then compare the two assessments. If exposure occurred first, record a second check following exposure rather than independent confirmation.\n\nWhen review narrows a claim, preserve its stable Claim ID if its scientific identity remains the same and record both original and current wording, the reason/date, and User disposition. Use child IDs for a split claim and a new ID for a materially different replacement. For manuscript-linked claims, reference a versioned Claim Control Object revision/digest rather than relying on mutable paragraph or page positions; citation-only and wording changes update that control object and remain in the artifact diff chain."),
])

p = Path("tests/test_citation_ledger_contract.py")
text = p.read_text()
anchor = "        self.assertIn(\"Source-level access or support for one proposition never validates other claims\", text)\n"
addition = anchor + "\n    def test_version_pinning_blinding_and_claim_control_are_required(self):\n        protocol = (ROOT / \"protocol/01.work-contract.md\").read_text()\n        notion = (ROOT / \"docs/notion-setup.md\").read_text()\n        skill = (ROOT / \"skills/scuter/SKILL.md\").read_text()\n        review = (ROOT / \"docs/record-and-review.md\").read_text()\n        for text in (protocol, notion, skill, review):\n            self.assertIn(\"Claim Control Object\", text)\n            self.assertIn(\"stable Claim ID\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"content digest\", protocol)\n        self.assertIn(\"prospectively blinded by construction\", protocol)\n        self.assertIn(\"Blinded second check/date\", notion)\n        self.assertIn(\"original and current wording\", notion)\n        self.assertIn(\"does not satisfy the independent second-check requirement\", skill)\n"
if text.count(anchor) != 1:
    raise SystemExit(f"test anchor: expected 1 match, found {text.count(anchor)}")
p.write_text(text.replace(anchor, addition, 1))
